{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/8f2l476d","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":170,"top":680,"width":2220,"height":200},"name":"body-1","text":"Tool results can guide its next action.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":76,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#24282E","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/vitkfm5o","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":170,"top":1260,"width":2210,"height":100},"name":"foot","text":"A tool can search a document, calculate a result, or change a file.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":45,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#5E636B","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/uhk36h4j","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":2430,"top":1370,"width":90,"height":50},"name":"page-number","text":"2","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":29,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#62676E","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/17h6mq","slideIndex":1,"text":"Time: 2 minutes.\n\nAn agent is a system that uses a model to select actions during a task. A tool is software the system can call. A tool result supplies new information.\n\nThe system can then take another action or return an answer. Sources: sources/work/LLMAndPrompt.key, slides 49 to 51; https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/building-effective-agents."}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/j1zcl6","slideIndex":2,"layout":{"id":"ly/pon6xgne","name":"Blank"},"title":"A tool returns a result","textShapes":4,"backgroundColor":"rgba(255,255,255,1)"}
